A declaration that *is* a host identifier is not emitted, in Go as in the other
two languages.

Every call to one became a call to that identifier, so a declaration would be
read by nobody. What was emitted instead is the body the *checker* synthesizes
for a bodyless func -- `return <zero>` -- which reads exactly like an
implementation and is the reason nobody noticed. JavaScript got the rule first;
Kotlin had it until a `deny` caught `fun hyp(a: Double, b: Double): Double = 0.0`
beside a working call; this is Go, the third.

Two marks, one rule. `#[go.native]` names a Go identifier and `#[cnative]` names
a C one -- C is an ABI rather than a target, so the mark names no language and
any backend that can call C reads it. They differ in nothing this fixture is
about: both land on `ir.Foreign` with `Marked` unset, which is the single test
`CodegenCtx.AllFuncs` applies. `#[foreign]` without the `native` flag sets
`Marked`, says the backend emits the declaration, and is deliberately untouched.

A `#[cnative]` on bubbletea rather than on gtk4 is the point: the *mark* decides
this, not the platform that usually carries it.

`sleep` returns nothing, so the checker synthesized an empty block for it and
the `len(fn.Block) == 0` guard every Go emitter already had skipped it. Only a
native with a *return type* ever grew a stub, which is why a fixture holding one
of each is what states the rule.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `func .*[Hh]ostname\(\) string \{` -- #[go.native] is os.Hostname at every call site; a declaration here would be a second one returning the zero value. Either case: bubbletea emits a free func under an exported name and a component's under its own
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `func .*Cabs\(n int\) int \{` -- #[cnative] is C.abs at every call site, and the same rule reaches it
broken out/go/bubbletea -- #[cnative] emits C.abs into model.go with no cgo preamble, so `C` is undefined
-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import macro "sngl:macro"
import go "sngl:language/go"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
    }
}

#[go.native("os", "os.Hostname", fails)]
func hostname() string

#[go.native("time", "time.Sleep")]
func sleep(ns int)

#[macro.cnative("abs")]
func cabs(n int) int

component main ui.node {
    var name = "idle"
    var v = 0

    ui.button(text="go", @click {
        sleep(1)
        name = hostname()
        v = cabs(v - 5)
    })

    ui.text(value="{name} {v}")
}

ui.window #w(title="native") {
    main()
}
